231	    /// spins for `spin_time` and `sleep_time` together. The consumer wakes all sleeping producers
232	    /// at once, at each half segment of releases. A sleep that ends early, woken for a slot another
233	    /// producer took, sleeps again to the same deadline, and `send_spin_sleep` looks at the ring
234	    /// once more after the last sleep.
235	    ///
236	    /// `send_spin_sleep` is available on Linux, and on other targets with the `std` feature, which
237	    /// provides its clock.
238	    ///
239	    /// # Parameters
240	    ///
241	    /// - `self`: this producer, by shared reference, so one handle may be used from several threads
242	    ///   at once.
243	    /// - `spin_time`: how long to spin while the ring is full, before sleeping. [`Ticks::ZERO`]
244	    ///   sleeps at once, and [`Ticks::FOREVER`] never sleeps.
